    "id": "AAMI-pds-strata-25",
    "content": "### Definitions — Loss\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**Loss** means the amount payable to compensate another lot owner in respect of a claim for a wrongful act, including damages, judgments, settlements, orders for costs and defence costs.\nYou has the meaning set out on page 11 and includes any office bearer.\nLimit The most we’ll pay under this cover in total for all claims in the period of insurance (including legal costs) is $1,000.\nLock replacement We cover You can make a claim under this cover independently of a claim for loss or damage to the strata building (including common property) or common contents.\nWe’ll cover the reasonable and necessary costs of replacing the strata building’s locks or changing the key codes if all of the following occurs:\n- keys or key codes to the common areas of the strata building are stolen from the insured address during the period of insurance\n- the keys or key codes have the address of the strata building on them\n- the theft is reported to the police.\nIf you make a claim under this additional cover no excess applies. We’ll settle the claim by paying you by direct deposit. This means that we won’t repair or replace or arrange for a service.\nWe don’t cover We don’t cover anything in section 3 ‘General exclusions’ see pages 31 to 44. We also don’t cover any of the following:\n- replacement of locks or key codes if you don’t report the theft to the police\n- replacement of motor vehicle or motorcycle keys or their locks\n- replacement of keys or key codes to lots or any lock which does not relate exclusively to the strata building or insured common contents\n- replacement of keys or key codes that were in the possession of a lot occupier Limit The most we will pay in total for any one incident is up to $1,000.",
