    "id": "ACENDA-pds-personal-protection--14",
    "content": "### Definitions — A longer benefit period\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**A longer benefit period** means your benefit can be paid for a longer period of time.\nYour premiums will cost more for shorter Waiting Periods.\nYour premiums will cost more for longer benefit periods.\nFor details see page 98.\n3. Choice of Indemnity or Agreed Value Indemnity cover - Your monthly benefit may be reduced because of a change in your Earnings.\nAgreed Value cover - Your monthly benefit won’t be reduced because of a change in your Earnings. Agreed Value cover will cost more than Indemnity cover for this reason.\nBoth are available under Income Protection Plus.\nIncome Protection Standard provides Indemnity cover only.\nAgreed Value and Indemnity cover is no longer available if you don’t already hold it. If you already hold Agreed Value or Indemnity cover, you can continue to make changes or transfer your cover (as set out in the PDS).\nFor details see pages 65 - 67.\nPersonal Protection Portfolio and Life Cover Super Product Disclosure Statement | 23 Income Protection insurance Income Protection insurance - Benefits, Features and Options Details are available at the page number listed.",
