    "id": "ACENDA-pds-acenda-insurance-1",
    "content": "### Definitions — Income Replacement Ratio Amount\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**Income Replacement Ratio Amount** means the amount described on page 75. Or the amount calculated by:\n- multiplying the relevant part of your Earnings Before Disability per annum with the percentage specified in the table below, and\n- dividing that amount by 12.\nEarnings Before Disability (per annum) %* First $300,000 70% From $300,001 to $500,000 50% From $500,001 (subject to the Maximum Income Protection Benefit of $30,000) 20% * If you have the Booster Option, 20% will be added to your percentage for up to 6 months.\nAcenda Insurance & Acenda Insurance (Super) Supplementary Product Disclosure Statement (SPDS) | 3 Acenda Insurance & Acenda Insurance (Super) Supplementary Product Disclosure Statement (SPDS) D. Income Assure insurance: Discontinuation of the Severe Disability Terms Removal Option The Severe Disability Terms Removal Option is no longer available under Income Assure insurance.\nLocation of change in the Insurance PDS Changes to the Insurance PDS The Severe Disability Terms Removal Option is deleted in the table of Benefits, Features and Options.\nThe options available under Income Assure is updated to:\nAvailable for Income Assure only Short Waiting Period for Accidental Injury Pages 87-88 INSIDE OUTSIDE SUPER The following ‘Severe Disability Terms Removal Option’ terms are deleted in the ‘Summary of the terms and conditions for Income Protection and Business Expenses’:\nSevere Disability Terms Removal Option (Available with Income Assure insurance only) If you have selected this Option, after two years on claim the definitions of Total Disability and Partial Disability will not require you to be Severely Disabled.",
