    "id": "ACENDA-pds-acenda-insurance-56",
    "content": "### Definitions — Transferring insurance\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**Transferring insurance** means replacing the insurance, either the full or part of the sum insured, with insurance on another policy. For example Income Protection outside super is replaced with Income Protection inside super.\nHow you can restore your Suspended Amount at the end of the Suspension Period We will notify you prior to the end of the Suspension Period and you can restore all or part of the Suspended Amount.\nThe amount restored will be the Restored Amount. There is no further medical or financial underwriting as the original disclosures you made at the time you applied for the insurance and any increase continue to apply.\nIf you direct that only part or none of the Suspended Amount be restored, your direction will be binding and cannot be amended 30 days after the end of the Suspension Period.\nIf you do not request an extension, we will automatically restore the full Suspended Amount to your insurance unless you have directed otherwise.\nIf you make a claim during the Suspension Period:\nSubject to these Cover Bounce-back terms, the terms of your insurance continue to apply during the Suspension Period.\nFor this feature only:",
