    "id": "ALLIANZ-pds-travel-insurance-5",
    "content": "### Definitions — An unforeseen medical event\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**An unforeseen medical event** means you need to change your journey. Your original trip costs are:\nFlights $2,000 Accommodation $1,000 If the death, injury or illness arises from a pre-existing medical condition, the most we will pay for all claims under subsection 3.1.1. e] will be:\nTo continue your journey you need to spend $2,500 for new flights and $500 on accommodation. Your airline gives you a full refund for the original flights and you are only able to get a $250 refund on your accommodation.\n$2,000 for Single cover type $2,000 per person for Duo cover type $4,000 for Family cover type Allowable claim:\nbut only if at the time of policy issue you were, or a reasonable person in your circumstances would have been, unaware of the likelihood of their dying or being admitted to hospital. No benefit is payable for additional travel and accommodation expenses arising from the pre-existing medical condition of a relative if you purchased a Basic Plan.\nFlights $500 - new flights $2,500 less refund of $2,000 from original flights Accommodation $750 - original accommodation of $1,000 less $250 is higher than new accommodation of $500.\nYour claimable amount will be $1,250.\nPlease call Allianz Global Assistance to confirm approval for these expenses.\nf] This will put you back in your original financial position.\nNote that any applicable excess will be deducted from the claimable amount.\nAdditional travel and accommodation expenses due to specified events If a disruption to your journey arises from any of the following reasons during the period of cover:\n3.1.2 What we do not cover To the extent permitted by law, we will not pay your claim if:",
