    "id": "ALLIANZ-pds-travel-insurance-27",
    "content": "### Definitions — Pre-existing medical condition\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**Pre-existing medical condition** means a condition of which a reasonable person in the circumstances, should have been aware at the time of issue of the Certificate of Insurance, including:\nany dental condition; or cash, bank notes, currency notes, cheques or negotiable instruments;\nany physical condition; or electronic data, software or intangible asset;\npregnancy; or watercraft of any type (other than surfboards);\nany lifelong illness; or furniture, furnishings, household appliances;\nany chronic illness; or hired items; or any mental illness; or any other item which may be listed as excluded on your Certificate of Insurance.\nany current or previously treated cancer, or any condition which, in the last two (2) years:\nMedical adviser was treated by surgery (including day surgery); or means a doctor (including a clinical psychologist) or dentist qualified to diagnose the condition or disorder, holding the necessary current certification in the country in which they are currently practising, and who is not you or your travel companion, or a relative or employee of you or your travel companion.\nrequired regular medication; or",
