    "content": "### excess payable under the policy applies to each\n\n**Clause Classification:** `SubLimit`\n\nearthquake and/or tsunami (including a series of earthquakes and/or tsunamis) that occurs during any consecutive 48-hour period. See Understanding your excesses on page 64.\n26 Insured Events ✗ Other general exclusions also apply – see What’s not covered? on page 51.\nSudden escape of liquid Buildings Insurance ✓ Contents Insurance ✓ What’s covered? What’s not covered? ✓ Loss or damage resulting directly from bursting, leaking, discharging or overflowing of any:\n✗ Loss or damage:\n- domestic appliances – for example a dishwasher or washing machine,\n- fixed rainwater or hot water tanks,\n- radiators and oil heaters,\n- fixed pipes, gutters or drainpipes, sinks, baths, basins or water carrying apparatus,\n- waterbeds, or\n- aquariums.\n- as a result of gradual escape of water or other liquid over time:\n» where you could reasonably be expected to have been aware of this such as, but not limited to, where there is visible damage and or changes to the property – for example, staining on ceilings or walls, evidence of mould or mildew, deterioration of tile grouting or adhesive, or » from a shower base, shower recess, shower alcove or the walls surrounding the shower.\nBuildings Insurance only If we have agreed to pay a claim for sudden escape of liquid to your buildings, we will also pay the costs of any exploratory work to locate the source of the damage if we have approved these costs before they are incurred. Please contact us to confirm approval. If you incur costs without our prior approval, we will only pay the reasonable covered costs up to the amount we would have agreed to, had you asked us first.\n- as a result of sinks, baths or basin overflowing due to:\n» a tap being left running, and » the plug being left in the drain.",
