    "id": "ALLIANZ-pds-policy-numbers-that--14",
    "content": "### What we cover\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Coverage`\n\n- theft or attempted theft When you take out your policy, we’ll agree on an amount with you that we’ll cover your car for. We call this the agreed value.\nIt’s up to you to decide how much cover you need. As a guide, it should be enough to replace your car if a covered incident happened and your car couldn’t be repaired.\n- weather events You will also need to factor in:\n- fire (including thermal runaway)\n- malicious damage What we don’t cover See page 42 for exclusions details.\nMore information Weather events can include cyclones, earthquakes, bushfires, storms, floods and hail.\nBattery thermal runaway for EVs is covered under fire, provided there has been no deviation from manufacturer specification in relation to battery usage and charging.\nWe will however cover battery thermal runaway for EV’s under fire if any deviation from the manufacturer specification did not cause or contribute to the thermal runaway.\n- any modifications, options or accessories that have been made or added to the car\n- wall charger, charging cable and charging accessories including wall mount for EVs\n- GST\n- registration and any CTP insurance\n- on-road costs like stamp duty, dealer delivery, dealer warranty costs or transfer fees.\nYou can always find the agreed value in your policy details document.\nWhat we don’t cover See page 42 for full exclusions details.\nMore information You’ll need to check if your agreed value is appropriate at renewal.\nMarket value is only offered under our Comprehensive Essentials Car Insurance.\nYour Cover 22 Your Cover 23 Contents \u0007 \u0007Market value Comprehensive Comparison \u0007 not covered Comprehensive Essentials covered Third Party Property Damage not covered",
