    "id": "ALLIANZ-pds-policy-numbers-that--18",
    "content": "### Important Information — What we cover\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Coverage`\n\n- the collision was caused by someone else, and If your car is in a collision and you weren’t at fault, we’ll arrange a rental car to help keep you moving.\n- you can provide the name and residential address or phone number of the other person who caused the collision, or any other information that would reasonably allow us to identify the person so that we can exercise our rights of recovery, and Here’s how it works:\n- you don’t have to pay your excess, see Understanding your excess on page 57.\nWe’ll arrange a rental car of a similar size and type (not necessarily the same make) to your car through our provider depending on availability.\nIf we can’t get you one, we’ll pay you a travel allowance of $80 a day, for as long as we would have given you the rental car.\nIf your car has disability modifications that are required for your or your family’s disability we’ll increase the allowance to cover reasonable additional costs associated with daily travel required due to your disability.\nCollisions not meeting the above criteria such as damage by an animal or weather event do not classify as not-at-fault.\nYou should always call us for approval before arranging a rental car. If you don’t, we will pay for expenses up to the amount we would have authorised had you asked us first.\nContact us for approval before you incur any costs above the $80 daily limit. Without approval first, we’ll only pay up to the amount we would have authorised had you asked us first.\nLimits You’ll get a rental car for up to 30 days. The rental car stops before the 30 day limit when:\n- the damage is repaired and your car returned to you, or\n- we pay you the repair cost, or\n- where your car is a total loss, we either pay you the market value, agreed value or agree to replace your new car.",
