    "id": "BINGLE-pds-comprehensive-car-24",
    "content": "### Additional benefits\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Coverage`\n\nyy you refused to contribute as outlined in ‘Contribution to repairs’ on page 9 (below); or yy we’ve determined your car to be a total loss; or We’ll settle your claim or provide you with services under an additional benefit in accordance with that additional benefit. If we are covering fair and reasonable costs that you’ve already paid yourself, we will pay you that value, less an amount equal to any applicable Input Tax Credit.\nyy we didn’t provide you with a new car under the ‘New for Old’ option on page 5 (above).\nKeeping up with claims under the ‘Keep Mobile’ option When your car is a total loss If we determine your car to be a total loss and we didn’t provide you with a new car under the ‘New for Old’ option on page 5 (above), we’ll settle your claim by a total loss payment.\nWe’ll take ownership of your car, and we’re entitled to any salvage value it has, unless your credit provider has those entitlements. We’ll deduct unexpired registration and compulsory third party (CTP) insurance from your settlement.\nThis could sound a bit complicated so, in a nutshell, a total loss payment is calculated as follows:\nyy For claims under the ‘New for Old’ option where we weren’t able to provide you with a new car, the calculation of your total loss payment starts with the greater of either what it would have cost us to replace your car under the option or what we determine is your car’s market value. Otherwise, it starts with what we determine is your car’s market value;",
