    "id": "BUDGET_DIRECT-pds-income-protection-33",
    "content": "### Definitions — Waiting Period\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**Waiting Period** means the period you must wait before the monthly benefit becomes payable under the policy, as set out in your policy schedule. You can choose a waiting period of 30 days or 60 days. During the waiting period you must be unable to perform your usual occupation due to a serious illness or injury. The waiting period begins on the date you first consult a registered medical practitioner for the serious illness or injury giving rise to your claim and when you cease all work due to that serious illness or injury. At the end of the waiting period, if you are still suffering from the serious illness or injury, you will be able to receive monthly benefit payments, paid in arrears. No monthly benefit is payable for the waiting period.\nHow to contact us Need to get in touch with Budget Direct? by email: life.sales@budgetdirect.com.au on the web: budgetdirect.com.au on the phone: 1800 555 048 Budget Direct Life Insurance PO Box 342, Toowong QLD 4066 Budget Direct Life Insurance is brought to you by Hannover Life Re of Australasia Ltd (Hannover) ABN 37 062 395 484",
