    "id": "BUDGET_DIRECT-pds-life-1",
    "content": "### Definitions — Total and Permanent Disablement\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**Total and Permanent Disablement** means solely as a result of your Sickness or Injury (whether physical or mental):\nA\n- The cover amount being issued by us is the same or less than that under the replaced policy, and You have been absent from work (or have not performed Domestic Duties) for a continuous period of at least 3 months, and at the end of those 3 months, we are reasonably satisfied that your Sickness or Injury (whether physical or mental) makes it unlikely that you will:\n- No claim is payable or pending or entitled to be made under the replaced cover.\n- If the ‘Own’ occupation definition applies: ever again engage in your own Occupation.\n- If the ‘Any’ occupation definition applies: ever again engage in any gainful employment for which you are reasonably qualified by education, training or experience.\n- If the ‘Domestic Duties’ definition applies: ever again be able to perform your usual unpaid Domestic Duties, or Where your cover has replaced another cover issued by us or another insurer and the sum insured under your cover is greater than the sum insured under the replaced cover, then the suicide exclusion will apply to the difference in the sums insured, from the commencement of your cover.\nBenefit Reductions The Death Benefit (including where it is paid as the Terminal Illness Benefit) is reduced by any amounts we pay under the optional Total and Permanent Disablement insurance cover and/or the optional Trauma Insurance cover.",
