    "content": "### Definitions — Serious illness or injury\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**Serious illness or injury** means due to an illness or an injury occurring after the commencement date, you are;\n\u0007 4 Unable to perform the usual duties of your usual occupation necessary to produce income.\n4 You are under regular care and following advice of a medical practitioner, in relation to your illness or injury for which you are claiming.\n4 Suffering a loss of income, and 4 not engaged in your usual occupation or any other gainful occupation.\nA serious illness or injury must be certified by your medical practitioner and confirmed by one or more medical specialists nominated by us.\nFor exclusions refer to the section ‘Do exclusions apply to Budget Direct Income Protection Cover?’ on page 7.",
