    "id": "COVER_MORE-pds-travel-22",
    "content": "### excess on the International Comprehensive plan, and claim\n\n**Clause Classification:** `SubLimit`\n\nfor Additional accommodation costs and cancellation costs because You were diagnosed with COVID-19 on Your overseas trip, We would deduct an excess of $750 in total from Your claim. ($250 excess + $500 special excess).\n2. Limits of liability The limits of Our liability for each Section of the policy are the amounts shown in the relevant table for the plan purchased as shown on pages 3-9 except:\nwhere the policy limit for SECTION 4: Amendment or Cancellation Costs applies on a per policy basis and will be shown on Your Certificate of Insurance;\nb) the maximum liability collectively for Sections 15, 16 and 17, shall not exceed $45,000 on the Comprehensive+ and $30,000 on the Comprehensive and Inbound plans;\nc) where You have paid the additional premium to include Cruise Cover on the International or Inbound plans, the standard benefits apply as per the plan purchased and the Cruise Cover additional benefits and limits apply (see pages 42-43);\nPolicy conditions d) 1. Excess where We have notified You in writing of different limits; or e) in some circumstances, prior to Your entry into the policy or when You apply for cover for Your Existing Medical Conditions, whichever occurs later, We may impose an additional of higher excess for claims arising from Existing Medical Conditions. We will inform You in writing if this applies: These will be set out in Your Certificate of Insurance or in a letter from Our medical assessment team.\nf) where the amount covered for Cancellation Plus Cover is limited as per the policy wording on page 13 and applies on a per policy basis.\n“Unattended” means not on Your person or within Your sight and reach.\n“Valuables” means articles made of or containing gold, silver or precious metals; binoculars; jewellery; mobile phones;",
