    "content": "### Definitions — Flood (Part 2)\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\nLoss and/or damage loss means physical loss and damage means physical damage, unless stated otherwise in your policy.\n\n#### CRITICAL POLICY EXCLUSIONS & LIMITATIONS (WHAT IS NOT COVERED):\n- Actions of the Sea & Storm Surge: Loss or damage caused by high tide, king tides, tidal waves, ocean rise, or actions of the sea is excluded.\n- Rainwater Run-off Demarcation: Surface rainwater run-off escaping over normally dry land (rather than from a natural watercourse, lake, canal, reservoir, or dam) is assessed under Insured Event 3 (Storm cover), not Flood.\n\n> ⚠️ **Mandatory Embargo Window:** A strict **72-hour embargo** applies post-purchase. No cover for losses occurring within 72 hours of policy inception unless transferring without lapse.",
