    "id": "HCF_LIFE-pds-cash-back-cover-6",
    "content": "### Definitions — Major Organ Transplant\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**Major Organ Transplant** means the medically necessary organ transplant from a donor to the Insured Person of 1 or more of the following organs: kidney, liver, heart, lung, pancreas or the transplanting of bone marrow.\nThe transplant of all other organs, parts of organs or any other tissue transplant is excluded.\nHOW A WAITING PERIOD WORKS HOW WE ASSESS THE WAITING PERIOD COVER COMMENCEMENT DATE 12 MONTHS The Waiting Period applies to the following Impairments:\n- Cancer of Specified Severity;\n- Kidney Failure;\n- Coronary Artery Bypass Graft Surgery;\n- Heart Attack of Specified Severity;\n- Stroke; and\n- Major Organ Transplant.\nThis means that if you suffer one of these Impairments within the first 12 months of the Cover Commencement Date, you will not be covered.\nThis also includes diagnosis, which means that if you are diagnosed with one of these Impairments within the first 12 months of the Cover Commencement Date, you will not be covered.\nEXAMPLES OF HOW A WAITING PERIOD WORKS APPROVED EXAMPLE DECLINED EXAMPLE Susan suffered from renal disease.\nShe continued to have symptoms or was receiving treatment in the years before taking out cover. Susan subsequently suffered Kidney Failure 2 years after her Cover Commencement Date.\nJames suffered from renal disease.\nHe continued to have symptoms or was receiving treatment in the years before taking out cover. James subsequently suffered Kidney Failure 6 months after his Cover Commencement Date.\nSusan submitted a claim which was approved because her Kidney Failure occurred more than 12 months after the Cover Commencement Date, which means that the Waiting Period does not apply.",
