    "id": "NEOS-pds-neos-protection-29",
    "content": "### Definitions\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\nConversion of Child Cover Benefit When the insured child approaches the expiry age for Child Cover, they have the option of converting their existing cover to Life Cover. They may also choose to attach or link Critical Illness Cover, without having to reapply or supply medical evidence to us.\nTo be eligible for this option, the insured child must exercise it:\n- before their Child Cover expires or is cancelled; and\n- when they’re 18 or 19 years old.\nThe sum insured on their new cover can be up to the same sum insured that applied under their Child Cover at the time it expired.\nTheir new premium will be based on their age and the current premium rates at the time the new cover is issued.\nAny exclusions which applied to their Child Cover will also be applied to their new cover.\nOther included benefits The following additional benefits included in Child Cover are described in the section, ‘Benefits common to Life Cover, TPD Cover and Critical Illness Cover’ from page 30 of this PDS. When reading this section, substitute references to ‘you’ and ‘your’ with ‘insured child’.\n- Indexation Benefit\n- Accommodation Benefit\n- Suspending Cover Benefit.",
