    "id": "PPS_MUTUAL-pds-professionals-choice-27",
    "content": "### Definitions — General Cover (super) TPD (Part 4)\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n- permanent loss in both eyes; or severe cognitive loss – permanent from age 70 Min. Sum Insured at Entry Benefit in detail Flexibility Features Indexation for Professionals Benefit p29 Your sum insured will automatically increase by the higher of the increase in the Professionals Earning Index, the increase in CPI or 3% each year (you can elect not to take the increase) $100,000 Premium Freeze Benefit Variable age-stepped premiums increase each year. This feature allows you to keep the cost of your insurance constant each year by decreasing your sum insured Max. Sum Insured at Entry Future Increases Benefit p30 You can increase your sum insured after certain specified events without having to provide further medical evidence $2,000,000 *Expiry and conversion will occur at the Plan anniversary following the relevant age *All references above to age refer to the current age of the Life Insured p29 Suspending Insurance Benefit p31 You can suspend your insurance upon request for up to 12 months (over the life of the insurance) Linking Options By linking your insurances, you can obtain a lower premium as a claim under one linked insurance will reduce the sum insured of the other linked insurance p10 Life Insurance Reinstatement after One Year Benefit If you have claimed on your Trauma Insurance that is linked to Life Insurance you can reinstate your Life Insurance one year from the time of claim p31 PROFESSIONALS CHOICE PRODUCT DISCLOSURE STATEMENT LIFE TPD TRAUMA ADDITIONAL INSURANCES INCOME PROTECTION BUSINESS EXPENSES INSURANCE PROFIT-SHARE PLAN ADDITIONAL INFORMATION",
