    "id": "QBE-pds-farm-12",
    "content": "### Excess Type\n\n**Clause Classification:** `SubLimit`\n\nIf you are unable to provide us with the full name and address of the person responsible for the incident, we are unable to waive the excess. We need these details in order to be able to conduct a settlement or recovery.\nWhere your vehicle is a total loss, and your claim is accepted, your Policy comes to an end. How your claim is settled will depend on whether you have taken out an agreed value policy or a market value policy.\n(a) If a security interest is registered over your vehicle, we will:\n(i) pay the financier the sum insured, up to the amount required to discharge your loan or finance agreement; and\n(ii) pay you the remaining balance of the settlement sum.\nAge or inexperienced driver\n(b) If no security interest is registered over your vehicle, we will:\n(i) pay you the sum insured; or\n(ii) replace your vehicle if a similar make and model is available.\nYou will not have to pay this additional excess if the only damage to your vehicle is a broken windscreen or window glass or is caused by storm or hail, or your vehicle is damaged while parked or unattended.\nLearner driver Each excess is shown in your Policy Schedule and is explained below.\n- in some instances, we’ll ask you to pay your excess to us such as where a repairer or supplier is not able to accept an excess payment or your vehicle is a total loss and we replace it with a new one;\n- if we pay you the reasonable cost to repair your vehicle, we will deduct the excess from the amount we pay you;\n- if your vehicle is a total loss and we pay you the agreed or market value for your car, we will deduct the excess from the amount we pay you.\nApplies to passenger vehicles only If a licensed learner driver is in control of your vehicle at the time of an accident, we apply the",
