    "id": "RAC_WA-pds-life-31",
    "content": "### Definitions — Waiting Period -\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**Waiting Period -** means the waiting period as stated on the Policy Schedule, and is the number of days at the beginning of a period of Total Disability, in respect of which no Total Disability benefit is payable. The Waiting Period begins on the Disablement Date. The Benefit Period for Total Disability commences after the completion of the Waiting Period.\nThis PDS should be read before making a decision to acquire or continue to hold RAC Income Protect. It is intended to help you decide whether RAC Income Protect will meet your needs and compare it with other products you may be considering. Any financial product advice contained in this PDS is of a general nature only and has been prepared without taking into account your objectives, financial situation and needs, so you should consider its appropriateness in the context of such factors.\nThis PDS and the RAC Income Protect product described within it are issued by AIA Australia Limited ABN 79 004 837 861, AFSL 230043 (AIA Australia).\nAIA Australia is a subsidiary of the AIA Group, has been operating in Australia for over 40 years and is registered by the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority (APRA). AIA Australia takes full responsibility for the entirety of this PDS and can be contacted at PO Box 6111, Melbourne, VIC, 3004 or on 1800 333 613.",
