    "id": "RACQ-pds-motor-18",
    "content": "### Excess free glass repair\n\n**Clause Classification:** `SubLimit`\n\nOptional for Car You are covered for:\nIf the ‘Excess free glass repair’ optional benefit is shown as ticked on your COI, you won’t have to pay an excess when you make a claim as long as:\n- the incident occurs within the period of insurance,\n- the claim is only for damage to your vehicle’s windscreen, window glass or sunroof glass and\n- you have not already claimed for this benefit during the period of insurance.\nLimit:\nS One glass repair or replacement in your period of insurance.\nYou are not covered for:\nDamage to any other glass which forms part of your vehicle, for example a fixed glass roof panel.\nDamage that doesn’t extend through the entire thickness of the windscreen, window glass, or sunroof glass.\nAdditional hire car Optional for Car You are covered for:\nIf the ‘Additional hire car’ optional benefit is shown as ticked on your COI and you are unable to use your vehicle as the result of an incident, we will pay for the costs for you to hire a car chosen by us to replace your vehicle.\nIf we are unable to arrange a hire car for you or a hire car does not suit your needs, we will pay for the costs for you to use an alternative mode of transport, such as taxis, rideshare or public transport.\nPage 30 | Motor Vehicle Insurance Policy Limit:\nS Up to $75 per day for up to 21 days of hire or alternative mode of transport.\nCoverage under this optional benefit will end if:\n- your vehicle is repaired and ready to be collected by you,\n- we settle and pay your claim as a total loss or\n- you exhaust the benefit limit.\nYou are not covered for:\nYour Cover If your vehicle is:\n- a veteran, vintage, classic or historic vehicle,\n- a motorhome or campervan or\n- designed to carry 2.5 tonnes or more.\nLoss, damage or legal liability which results from you using a hire car or alternative mode of transport.",
