    "content": "### Exclusions and General Exclusions)\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Exclusion`\n\n- Limits under each section of cover\n- \u0007 Your obligations, including what You need to tell Us when You apply, and what to do when You need to make a claim;\nand\n- Other things You need to know about Your insurance.\nTravel Insurance Combined Financial Services Guide And Product Disclosure Statement (including policy wording) | 3 Summary of Cover We know that all travellers do not have the same needs, which is why We have designed a number of travel insurance plans including International, Annual Multi-Trip and Domestic, as well as giving You the ability to add optional extras. All plans cover 2 Adults and Your Children and Grandchildren.\nWe have published a series of Target Market Determinations which outline the target market intended to be suitable for each particular travel insurance plan We offer. A copy of the Target Market Determination can be found at www.tokiomarine.com.au Plan types Key benefits# Limits 3 International Single Trip options:\n24 hour emergency assistance\n- Comprehensive\n- Essentials \u0007Sports and activities automatically included Each section has limits and sub limits that You should be aware of. A sub limit is a subset of the overall policy benefit section.\n- Basics 1 Annual Multi-Trip option 3 Domestic Single Trip options:\n- Comprehensive\n- Domestic Cancellation\n- Rental Car Excess Choice of excess You can choose to vary Your Excess.\nOur default Excess for international policies is $250 but can be reduced to $100 or $0 for an increased Premium. Our default Excess for Our domestic policies is $100 but can be reduced to $0 for an increased Premium. Your Excess will be shown on Your Certificate of Insurance.",
