    "id": "SHANNONS-pds-motor-1",
    "content": "### Excesses\n\n**Clause Classification:** `SubLimit`\n\nHow to pay your excess When your excess will be waived How we settle your claim Your repairs (choice of repairer) Our parts policy for authorised repairs Contribution to repairs If your vehicle has been stolen If your vehicle is a total loss Salvage After we pay your claim What happens with cancellations PDS preparation date 3/12/2020 Other Important Information Words with special meanings How to contact us with a complaint General insurance code of practice Motor car insurance and repair industry code of conduct Report insurance fraud INSURANCE FOR MOTORING ENTHUSIASTS INTRODUCTION WELCOME TO SHANNONS Shannons has specialised in insurance for motoring enthusiasts for over 40 years. We enjoy a unique relationship with motoring enthusiasts and our dedicated team is in place to offer you a knowledgeable personalised service.\nBy choosing Shannons you can:\nMake a claim 24/7 online or by calling 13 46 46 Call 13 46 46 for extra support Why is this document important? This Product Disclosure Statement (PDS) is an important document that contains details of your Shannons Motor Insurance if you purchase this product from us. It also explains in the ‘Important information about us’ statement (see page 8), certain information about the financial services we offer, how we are remunerated and what relationships we have with others, to help you decide if you would like to use the services we offer. This PDS also explains how we will deal with your complaint if you ever have a concern with your dealings with us.\nOur agreement with you If you buy this product from us, your contract of insurance is made up of your certificate, this PDS and any supplementary PDS (SPDS) that we have given you.\nYou may need to refer to this document from time to time, so keep it in a safe place.",
