    "id": "SCTI-pds-travelcare-36",
    "content": "### TravelCare SPDS — Important information about this SPDS\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Coverage`\n\nThis is a SPDS issued by Southern Cross Benefits Ltd, trading as Southern Cross Travel Insurance (SCTI), ABN 99 133 401 939, AFS Licence No 331058 that contains updates and additions to the International Comprehensive Single Trip Product Disclosure Statement (PDS), effective 12 July 2025.\nThis SPDS should be read together with the International Comprehensive Single Trip PDS and any other SPDS given to you by SCTI for your PDS. The PDS is amended by this document with effect from the date on which this SPDS is given to you. This SPDS was prepared on 1 July 2026 and applies to policies issued from 1 July 2026.\nChanges to the PDS The following TravelCare Delay Assist benefit is inserted beneath the red ‘What we won’t cover’ box on page 50.\nD.3.1A TravelCare Delay Assist We’ll provide you with a $40 digital voucher for you to use if your registered flight is delayed by two hours or more. This benefit applies to all eligible travellers if your registered flight is delayed during your journey. Receiving this benefit does not affect your ability to claim under your base policy, provided you meet the relevant conditions.\nAll terms, conditions, exclusions and definitions in your base policy also apply to this benefit unless expressly stated otherwise.",
