    "id": "SUNCORP-pds-home-contents-31",
    "content": "### Definitions — Personal valuables\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**Personal valuables** means items that are valuable personal belongings that are normally carried with you away from the insured address such as:\n- jewellery and watches\n- handbags and wallets\n- mobile phones, laptops, electronic tablets (for example, iPads)\n- portable electronic and electrical items and their accessories\n- sporting, recreational and leisure goods when not in use (however, not an e-bicycle, see ‘personal transportation vehicles’). However, we’ll cover bicycles while in use provided they’re not being used for racing or pace-making\n- photographic and optical equipment\n- a wheelchair, mobility scooter, or similar medical aids designed to assist with physical disabilities or the elderly\n- a motorised golf cart with 4 wheels.\nHowever, the following items can’t be insured as ‘Personal valuables – unspecified items’ and must be insured as ‘Personal valuables – specified items’ regardless of their value:\n- drones while not in use (see section 10 ‘Terms and words with special meanings (definitions)’ on page 109). There is no cover for drones while in use\n- personal transportation vehicles (see section 10 ‘Terms and words with special meanings (definitions)’ on page 112).\nPersonal valuables – specified items This cover is optional for the Classic, Classic Extras, and Classic Advantages levels of cover.\nWe cover We’ll cover accidental loss or damage to Personal valuables – specified items at or away from the insured address during the period of insurance, anywhere in Australia or New Zealand.\nWe’ll also cover jewellery and watches anywhere in the world for up to 30 consecutive days, however, only while being worn by you or while in a secure safe.",
