    "id": "SUNCORP-pds-home-contents-insura-18",
    "content": "### Definitions — Secure\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**Secure** means your contents are stored in a storage unit or compartment that:\n–– is lockable and –– only you or someone you authorised has access to it and –– is fully enclosed by walls (including doors) floor and roof.\nIf you plan on keeping your contents in storage for longer than 365 days, contact us to find out your insurance choices for covering contents in storage for longer periods.\nWe do not cover –– cash or documents able to be cashed –– jewellery –– contents in storage away from your insured address for longer than 365 days –– l\u0007oss or damage to contents in storage after your contents policy at the insured address ceases –– theft when there is no forced entry into your storage facility –– contents stored outside Australia –– contents in an unsecured storage facility –– contents not stored in a commercially operated facility.\n10. Replacement of locks We cover When you have home or contents cover, we will pay the necessary cost of replacing locks to the external doors or windows of your home or unit or changing their key codes if keys to those locks are stolen anywhere in Australia or New Zealand.\nThe limit is $500 for any incident resulting in a claim.\nSuncorp Insurance 11. Mortgage discharge costs We cover When you have home cover and we pay a claim for your home to a credit provider that fully repays your home loan, then we will pay the administrative and legal costs of:\n–– discharging the mortgage and –– deleting the mortgagee from the land title on your home.\nThe most we will pay under this additional feature in any one period of insurance is $1,000.\nWe do not cover Penalty interest rate charges or early loan repayment charges imposed on you by the credit provider.",
