    "id": "TAL-pds-group-plus-13",
    "content": "### Definitions — Date of Claim\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**Date of Claim** means the later of the following:\na. the date the Insured Person ceases to work due to Illness or Injury; and b. the date a Medical Practitioner has stated, in a written format acceptable to us, as being the date that the Insured Person suffered from the Illness or Injury that is the principal cause of the Insured Person’s inability to work.\nIf (b) is less than seven days after (a) then the Waiting Period will commence on the date determined under (a) otherwise it will be the date determined under (b).\nDSM Eligibility Criteria b. any other form of financial imposition levied under any law of a State or Territory or under the laws of the Commonwealth of Australia.\nHealth Insurance",
