    "content": "### what is not covered and any for limits that apply please read\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Exclusion`\n\nyour Schedule and this PDS including the “when we will not pay your claim” section.\nCaravan Camper trailer Horse trailer Trailer ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✘ ✘ ✔ ✔ ✘ ✘ ✔ ✔ ✘ ✘ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✘ ✘ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ ✔ Caravan Camper trailer Horse trailer Trailer ✔ ✔ ✘ ✘ ✔ ✔ ✘ ✘ Table of Contents page Territory Caravan and Trailer Insurance\b Summary of policy features and benefits\b Our agreement with you\b Your waiting period for cyclone, flood and bush fire\b Your premium\b Fourteen day cooling off period\b Assigning your rights and appointing a representative\b Governing law\b Duty of Disclosure\b Your No Claim Bonus (NCB) or Rating level\b Comprehensive caravan and trailer insurance\b 14 Optional benefits\b Making a claim\b How we will settle your claim\b Choosing a repairer\b Parts used to repair your caravan or trailer\b page Excesses/deductions\b Other deductions\b When we will not pay your claim\b Changes to your policy\b Cancellation rights under your policy\b How to resolve a complaint\b Privacy notice\b How we collect your personal information\b General Insurance Code of Practice\b If this insurance has been issued through an insurance intermediary\b Financial Claims Scheme\b Updating this PDS\b Phoning for assistance and conﬁrmation of transactions\b Words with special meanings\b Our agreement with you Your insurance contract When you buy our caravan and trailer insurance, we enter into a contract with you that is called the policy which is made up of:\n- your policy schedule;\n- this Product Disclosure Statement (PDS),\n- any applicable Supplementary PDS (SPDS) we issue that varies the PDS; and\n- any other document we tell you forms part of the policy at or prior to entry into your insurance contract or when required or permitted by law.",
