    "id": "TID-pds-travel-28",
    "content": "### Definitions — Pregnancy-related\n\n**Clause Classification:** `Definition`\n\n**Pregnancy-related** means your suitcases, trunks and similar containers (including their contents), articles worn or carried by you, and sporting equipment. It does not mean or include any:\n- bicycle;\nmeans arising from or directly connected with the process and changes in a mother resulting from a developing foetus. It covers the mother and foetus, as per the limits and conditions of cover set out in this policy, when either requires emergency medical care.\n- business samples or items that you intend to trade;\nPre-existing medical condition\n- valuables;\n- snow sport equipment;\n- passport or travel documents;\nmeans a condition of which a reasonable person in the circumstances, should have been aware at the time of issue of the Certiﬁcate of Insurance, including:\n- cash, bank notes, currency notes, cheques or negotiable instruments;\n- any dental condition; or\n- any physical condition; or\n- electronic data, software or intangible asset;\n- pregnancy; or\n- watercraft of any type (other than surfboards);\n- any lifelong illness; or\n- furniture, furnishings, household appliances;\n- any chronic illness; or\n- hired items; or\n- any mental illness; or\n- any other item which may be listed as excluded on your Certiﬁcate of Insurance.\nany current or previously treated cancer, or any condition which, in the last two (2) years:\nMedical adviser\n- was treated by surgery (including day surgery); or means a doctor (including a clinical psychologist) or dentist qualiﬁed to diagnose the condition or disorder, holding the necessary current certiﬁcation in the country in which they are currently practising, and who is not you or your travel companion, or a relative or employee of you or your travel companion.\n- required regular medication; or\n- required on-going treatment; or",
