    "id": "YOUI-pds-home-28",
    "content": "### excess within 72 hours of a flood occurring, cover will be limited (Part 11)\n\n**Clause Classification:** `SubLimit`\n\nAccidental Broken Glass and Ceramics What is covered? Table of contents pg. 3 ↗ Product guide pg. 4 ↗ Start of section pg. 28 ↗ The cost of replacing accidentally broken glass or ceramics which:\n- i\u0007s fitted at the premises, including sky lights, if you have buildings cover with us; or\n- forms part of your contents if you have contents cover with us.\nWe will also pay the cost:\n- of reconnecting any electrical components; and\n- \u0007to repair or replace picture, mirror or window frames or housings where necessary.\nThe most we will pay for each claim is 10% of the buildings sum insured after excess, or 10% of the contents sum insured after excess.\nBroken glass or ceramics as a result of an insured event is covered under Insured Events and these limits do not apply.\nWhat is not covered? The following exclusions do not apply where Optional Cover:\nContents Accidental Loss or Damage or Optional Cover:\nBuildings Accidental Damage has been added to your policy.\nLoss or damage to:\n- light bulbs or tubes;\n- a glasshouse or conservatory;\n- cooking or heating appliances;\n- \u0007any items outside your private domestic residence;\n- tiles;\n- \u0007a television, computer or any other electronic device or appliance with a display screen; or\n- \u0007your buildings or contents caused by accidentally broken glass or ceramics.\nBreakages such as scratches, chips or cracks, that do not extend through the entire thickness of the item.\nHome Insurance • About your cover 7.\nLocks and Keys What is covered? Table of contents pg. 3 ↗ The cost of replacing the locks and/or keys to the external doors or windows of your buildings if the keys to your buildings are stolen.\nProduct guide pg. 4 ↗ Start of section pg. 28 ↗ The most we will pay for each claim is $1,000 after excess.\n\n#### CRITICAL POLICY EXCLUSIONS & LIMITATIONS (WHAT IS NOT COVERED):\n- Actions of the Sea & Storm Surge: Loss or damage caused by high tide, king tides, tidal waves, ocean rise, or actions of the sea is excluded.\n- Rainwater Run-off Demarcation: Surface rainwater run-off escaping over normally dry land (rather than from a natural watercourse, lake, canal, reservoir, or dam) is assessed under Insured Event 3 (Storm cover), not Flood.\n\n> ⚠️ **Mandatory Embargo Window:** A strict **72-hour embargo** applies post-purchase. No cover for losses occurring within 72 hours of policy inception unless transferring without lapse.",
